mployee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Energy Fuels Inc is a small-cap energy business with a $1.7B market cap on $66M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +74% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -13% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $109M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -43.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 169% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 71/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Energy peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 479% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Energy Fuels (UUUU) Is Considered a Good Investment by Brokers: Is That True?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/energy-fuels-uuuu-considered-good-133002389.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.816,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"UUUU Bets on Pinyon Plain to Meet 2026 Output Goals: Will It Pay Off?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/uuuu-bets-pinyon-plain-meet-130800565.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575280.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Is Energy Fuels (TSX:EFR) Balancing Uranium Deliveries and Rare Earth Plans?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/ca/stocks/metal-and-mining/how-is-energy-fuels-tsxefr-balancing-uranium-deliveries-and-rare-earth-plans","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794498180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment"